^edqtItemDrop1=These fields are used in core quest-drop logic. They are to allow players $B$Bget quest drop which is not quest delivery (ReqItem stand for this), $B$Bbut needed to create quest delivery by player. $B$BReqSourceId1 is the id of a source item for creation of ReqItemX. $B$BX is the value of ReqSourceRef1. Only items which are quest items $B$B(having QuestChance > 0 in *_loot_template) should be used as sources here. $B$BPlayer will be allowed to gather sources up to amount required for$B$B ReqItemCount1(ReqSourceRef1) creation. $B$B$B$BYou may define 1, 2, 3 or even all 4 sources for the same ReqItem or $B$Buse 4 sources for 4 ReqItems.
^edqtItemDrop2=These fields are used in core quest-drop logic. They are to allow players $B$Bget quest drop which is not quest delivery (ReqItem stand for this), $B$Bbut needed to create quest delivery by player. $B$BReqSourceId1 is the id of a source item for creation of ReqItemX. $B$BX is the value of ReqSourceRef1. Only items which are quest items $B$B(having QuestChance > 0 in *_loot_template) should be used as sources here. $B$BPlayer will be allowed to gather sources up to amount required for$B$B ReqItemCount1(ReqSourceRef1) creation. $B$B$B$BYou may define 1, 2, 3 or even all 4 sources for the same ReqItem or $B$Buse 4 sources for 4 ReqItems.
^edqtItemDrop3=These fields are used in core quest-drop logic. They are to allow players $B$Bget quest drop which is not quest delivery (ReqItem stand for this), $B$Bbut needed to create quest delivery by player. $B$BReqSourceId1 is the id of a source item for creation of ReqItemX. $B$BX is the value of ReqSourceRef1. Only items which are quest items $B$B(having QuestChance > 0 in *_loot_template) should be used as sources here. $B$BPlayer will be allowed to gather sources up to amount required for$B$B ReqItemCount1(ReqSourceRef1) creation. $B$B$B$BYou may define 1, 2, 3 or even all 4 sources for the same ReqItem or $B$Buse 4 sources for 4 ReqItems.
^edqtItemDrop4=These fields are used in core quest-drop logic. They are to allow players $B$Bget quest drop which is not quest delivery (ReqItem stand for this), $B$Bbut needed to create quest delivery by player. $B$BReqSourceId1 is the id of a source item for creation of ReqItemX. $B$BX is the value of ReqSourceRef1. Only items which are quest items $B$B(having QuestChance > 0 in *_loot_template) should be used as sources here. $B$BPlayer will be allowed to gather sources up to amount required for$B$B ReqItemCount1(ReqSourceRef1) creation. $B$B$B$BYou may define 1, 2, 3 or even all 4 sources for the same ReqItem or $B$Buse 4 sources for 4 ReqItems.
^edqtRequiredNpcOrGo4=(value > 0) 1.-4. required creature/gameobject ID the player $B$Bneed to kill/use in order to complete the quest.$B$BIf ReqSpellCastN > 0 then at ReqCreatureOrGOIdN $B$Bmust be casted spell ReqSpellCastN, if ReqSpellCastN = 0 $B$Bthen it must be killed.
^edqtRequiredNpcOrGo3=(value > 0) 1.-4. required creature/gameobject ID the player $B$Bneed to kill/use in order to complete the quest.$B$BIf ReqSpellCastN > 0 then at ReqCreatureOrGOIdN $B$Bmust be casted spell ReqSpellCastN, if ReqSpellCastN = 0 $B$Bthen it must be killed.
^edqtRequiredNpcOrGo2=(value > 0) 1.-4. required creature/gameobject ID the player $B$Bneed to kill/use in order to complete the quest.$B$BIf ReqSpellCastN > 0 then at ReqCreatureOrGOIdN $B$Bmust be casted spell ReqSpellCastN, if ReqSpellCastN = 0 $B$Bthen it must be killed.
^edqtRequiredNpcOrGo1=(value > 0) 1.-4. required creature/gameobject ID the player $B$Bneed to kill/use in order to complete the quest.$B$BIf ReqSpellCastN > 0 then at ReqCreatureOrGOIdN $B$Bmust be casted spell ReqSpellCastN, if ReqSpellCastN = 0 $B$Bthen it must be killed.
